                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Gun Wings is a very very difficult shoot ‘em up, being a bullet hell of a game having a cast of three characters, each with their own unique style of shooting as well as a choice of fire pattern to add for a potential to have an ideal firing pattern to your liking. The game is a little on the short-side but it was an enjoyable experience for the time I played.\n\n[h1]Story[/h1]\nThe story is not the biggest side of the game, though its understandable as the concept of a shoot em up is the game-play, though the story goes that a giant meteor is headed towards Earth and it is up to three girls who had their bodies modified to be weapons are sent up to destroy the meteor and save humanity, who had recently rebuilt after an apocalypse that almost wiped it out.\n\n[h1]Game-play[/h1]\nVery chaotic! I’ve seen some bullet hell games, and this one is likely one of the more hectic ones,  though it can go from relatively tame to spiking up to extremely difficult at a moment’s notice. Going from Undertale bullet hell to Touhou bullet hell. One thing I did enjoy was that there were three different color schemed girls, red, yellow and blue, each able to absorb bullets of that color which charged their special attack, so it did make for an interesting play-through where your instinct was to dodge the bullets but also remember you can absorb some to help you out. The standard bullet hell with many enemies up until the boss and mini-bosses exists, so not really much to say on that, but one thing I did like is that this game allowed you to resume from your last spot you died, so you can still be bad at bullet hells and enjoy it, or even keep practicing without having to restart from the beginning each time.\n\n[h1]Visuals[/h1]\nIt looked nice at first, though some of the coloring was very bright and did hurt a little bit to look at for a while, but the game was visually pleasing and enjoyable to play. The music was a very upbeat with a relatively high tempo to keep you in that high intensity state of mind to help you stay alert and dodge the incoming bullets.\n\nOverall, this was a very entertaining game, even if this is not a genre I am well versed in, I did enjoy my playthrough, despite my numerous deaths, but again do keep it mind its relatively short length, as it took me about an hour to complete with numerous deaths.\n\nVerdict 7/10\n\nIf you enjoyed this review, please follow our curator [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/9673931/]here![/url]",
